## AUTH

# Lets any contact with no password credential sign in with the literal
# password "password". Needed for password login on a remote dev box, where the
# Google OAuth redirect cannot reach you. Opt-in in every environment — unset
# means denied, development included. Never set it on a deployment reachable
# from the internet: it applies to every contact without a password, which
# includes every Google-only account.
# AUTH_DEMO_CREDENTIALS_ENABLED=true











## Environment Configuration

### Development

# Where the dev servers are browsed from. Leave unset for a purely local
# clone — everything defaults to localhost. Set it when the dev servers run on
# a shared box you reach over Tailscale, and the auth/RPC URLs, CORS origins
# and each app's allowedHosts all follow. Scheme + host, no port and no
# trailing slash: each app appends its own port. The scheme is part of the
# value because the box can be fronted with TLS.
#
# This is the suffix root, not the central host. Generated domain hosts hang
# below it (demo.urm.test) and the platform is app. above them (app.urm.test),
# which a MagicDNS name cannot serve — point a Tailscale split-DNS nameserver
# at a resolver with a wildcard for this name.
# TAILSCALE_URL=http://urm.test

# Browser-visible config (apps/web, apps/docs)
#
# PUBLIC_ is the only prefix that reaches browser code: both apps are Astro,
# which sets Vite's envPrefix to PUBLIC_, so a VITE_-prefixed value is silently
# undefined at runtime. (The VITE_ names this file used to list were left over
# from apps/web being a Vite SPA.)
#
# Leave PUBLIC_AUTH_ISSUER origin-relative. src/pages/api/auth/[...path].ts
# proxies it to the API, so the session cookie stays first-party — every cookie
# is SameSite=Lax, and posting cross-site at the API host directly means the
# browser will not send it back. Relative also means a tenant host lands its own
# cookie instead of the central host's.
#
# This covers credential POSTs only. Google OAuth deliberately does NOT use it:
# /auth/google/authorize sets the PKCE cookie and /auth/google/callback reads it
# back, so both must be the API's own origin or every callback fails as
# invalid_state. That origin is derived from PUBLIC_RPC_URL below — which is
# why PUBLIC_RPC_URL must stay absolute and name the API.
PUBLIC_AUTH_ISSUER=/api/auth
PUBLIC_RPC_URL=http://localhost:1234/api/rpc

# .env file (apps/rpc/)
RPC_PORT=1234
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4321




# Remote development (these default to TAILSCALE_URL's host, so only set them
# to override):
# ADMIN_APP_URL=http://app.urm.test:4321
# MARKETING_APP_URL=http://urm.test:4321

### Production - Dedicated RPC Subdomain

# Web app environment (root domain)
PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://rpc.example.com

# RPC service environment
RPC_PORT=1234
RPC_PATH=/                    # Serve at root for dedicated subdomain
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com

### Production - Shared Domain with Path

# Web app environment (root domain)
PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://api.example.com/rpc

# RPC service environment
RPC_PORT=1234
RPC_PATH=/rpc                 # Serve at /rpc path
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com

### Environment Variables

# | Variable | Used By | Description | Example |
# |----------|---------|-------------|---------|
# | `PUBLIC_RPC_URL` | `apps/web`, `apps/docs` browser | Full URL for browser RPC calls | `https://rpc.example.com` |
# | `PUBLIC_AUTH_ISSUER` | `apps/web` browser | Auth base URL; relative keeps the cookie first-party | `/api/auth` |
# | `RPC_URL` | Web app (SSR) | Internal URL for server-side RPC | `http://rpc-service.internal:1234` |
# | `RPC_PORT` | RPC service | Port to listen on | `1234` |
# | `RPC_PATH` | RPC service | Path to serve RPC (use `/` for dedicated subdomain) | `/` or `/api/rpc` |
# | `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | RPC service | CORS allowed origins (comma-separated) | `https://example.com` or `https://example.com,https://tenant1.example.com` |

### CORS Configuration

# The RPC service automatically handles CORS:
# - Validates `Origin` header against `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`
# - Responds to `OPTIONS` preflight requests
# - Sets appropriate CORS headers for browser requests
# - Allows requests without origin (server-to-server SSR calls)

# When add tenant subdomains, just update ALLOWED_ORIGINS:
# # Current
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com
# # With tenants
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://tenant1.example.com,https://tenant2.example.com

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com"
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="GOCSPX-xxxxxx"

API_KEY=foo
ALCHEMY_PASSWORD=todo
